<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78235" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρακομ-ίζω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῐῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PPetr.</u>
					3p.122
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span> :—<i>escort, convoy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				125
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				1.4.7
			</span></i> :— 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Oth.</u>
				16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>carry</i> or <i>convey over, transport</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ Ὑπερβορέων εἰς Δῆλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					580a17
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ναῦς ἐπὶ τὸ χῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					50.6
				</span></i>
			 : generally, <i>convey, carry</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.147
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Med.
			, <i>have</i> a thing <i>brought one</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῖτον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					5.4.57
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.4.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Oth.</u>
				3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>obtain, receive</i> a document, Mitteis <i><span class="en">
				<u>Chr.</u>
				227.4
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>go</i> or <i>sail beside, coast along</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν Ἰταλίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.44
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρὰ τὴν ἤπειρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					48.27
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐς τὸν . . λιμένα, ἐπὶ
				Καμαρίνης</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.52
			</span></i> : abs., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Luc.</u>
				37
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>go</i> or <i>sail across, pass over</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.52.6
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
